NAME
    dir - list directory contents

SYNOPSIS
    dir [-R] [-S] [path | glob]

DESCRIPTION
    Lists a directory. With no argument it lists the current working
    directory; a path lists that directory; a glob (containing * or ?)
    lists the matching entries. Directories are shown with a trailing
    slash. dir is a /bin program.

    Entries are sorted within each directory (and, with -R, at every
    level). The default order is by name, raw ASCII -- so uppercase
    A-Z sort before lowercase a-z. -S sorts by byte size, largest
    first, with ties broken by name; a directory has no shown size and
    so counts as size 0, sorting after all files.

OPTIONS
    -R    list subdirectories recursively (like tree)
    -S    sort by file size, largest first (default is by name)

EXAMPLES
    dir              list the current directory, sorted by name
    dir /bin         list a directory by path
    dir -S           list the CWD, largest files first
    dir *.asm        entries in the CWD matching a glob
    dir /bin/*.bin   glob within another directory
    dir -R /sub      recursive listing of /sub
    dir -R -S /sub   recursive listing, each level size-sorted

SEE ALSO
    tree, find, cd, pwd, ls
